Fixes to usbipd-mac, applied by setup.sh on top of commit 1c2ab45 (the version it was
tested against). Without them a Xilinx Platform Cable USB II attaches but cannot
program an FPGA:

- USBIPStreamFramer: TCP does not keep the client's write boundaries, and the Linux
  usbip client sends the import request in two writes, so every import failed.
  Messages are now reassembled from the stream before being processed.
- ServerCoordinator: URBs ran on a concurrent queue, which reordered bulk OUT
  transfers and cut FPGA programming short. Each endpoint now gets a serial queue,
  and submits over the per-client limit are no longer dropped.

